# Valgrind suppressions for the nightly "Valgrind on built C output (subset)"
# step. Each entry must be scoped to one specific known frame and cite the
# upstream issue that makes it provisional. Remove an entry when its cited
# issue is fixed; do NOT broaden these to whole-library wildcards.
#
# The two chelis#406 entries (chelis_list_from_values / chelis_contiguous)
# were removed during the 0.18.5 bump: chelis#406 closed COMPLETED on
# 2026-06-19 and had been carried through two pin bumps since. Both frames
# are reachable in this lane's grad_quadratic program, so the nightly is a
# real re-probe rather than a formality. If it goes red, the leak is a live
# residual -- file it and cite the new issue here, do not re-add a
# suppression for a closed one.

# Not a chelis bug: libgomp allocates per-thread TLS in the OpenMP worker pool
# (GOMP_parallel) that is never freed at process exit. This is the standard
# OpenMP-runtime valgrind false positive, independent of chelis.
{
   libgomp-thread-pool-tls
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:calloc
   fun:calloc
   fun:allocate_dtv
   fun:_dl_allocate_tls
   ...
   fun:GOMP_parallel
}
